cff-version: 1.2.0

message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata provided below.

title: >-
  ABCC Bioinformatics Faba Bean Image Classification Repository: A Reproducible Image Classification Pipeline on Faba Beans

type: software

version: "1.0.0"

date-released: "2025-09-11"

license: MIT

repository-code: "https://github.com/AAFC-Bioinfo-AAC/faba-bean-image-classification"

abstract: >-
  This work provides a workflow for running faba bean feature extraction
  pipeline to extract the dimensional, shape and color of faba bean seeds
  in the .csv file from the faba bean images. It presents a methodology 
  for seed image segmentation and feature extraction using advanced
  deep learning and image processing techniques. The Segment Anything 
  Model 2.1 (SAM2.1) has been used for precise segmentation, while OpenCV, 
  Scikit-Image, and Matplotlib-colors are employed to analyze the dimensional,
  spatial, shape, and color properties of segmented seeds. The pipeline also 
  gives the seed count in an image and annotated binary images. The pipeline 
  has been specifically developed based on the spatial coordinates of
  faba bean seeds, colorcard, label, ruler and coin.

keywords:
  - Faba bean
  - Feature extraction
  - Image analysis
  - Deep learning
  - Phenotyping
  - SAM2.1 (Segment Anything Model 2.1)
  - TGW (Thousand Grain Weight)
  - SMP-UNet
  - Phenotypic analysis
  - Image segmentation
  - OpenCV
  - Scikit-Image
  - reproducibility
  - bioinformatics
  - pipeline
  - AAFC

